From 3e18cdd685568294084a1fceb6427ffbb5af757e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 02:11:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: mediatek: trace CPU9 CPU_ON substages

The first CPU9 attempt after repairing the CPU-hotplug lock
recursion opens the CPU9 ledger, completes PRESTATE, and stops
inside its CPU_ON binder operation. The current retained records
cannot distinguish P30E prepare, membership begin, P30E arm, or
the existing CPU boot callback.

Use the still-empty fourth ramoops record for eight ordered
before/after checkpoints around those exact calls. Require the
CPU9 transition ledger at BEFORE CPU_ON before claiming the lane,
and fail closed on any diagnostic error.

This does not add a CPU request, CPU_OFF, retry, cluster effect,
reset, storage, or boot-policy path.
